{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour Python store-test modules contain 22 audited prose blocks with incident history, duplicated consolidation rationale, or ornamental section banners. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@50716c9aed87479e4347a4daf084c9778c8793f7`. Two old ranges each contained both a section-comment block and a function docstring; the stable IDs below count them independently.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the 22 allowlisted true leading docstrings and contiguous full-line comment blocks. Capture immutable before/final blobs and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` nodes from `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, and `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require normalized AST equality.\n\nTokenize comments by enclosing symbol plus the next unchanged executable anchor. Reject changes to every inline comment, directive, and non-allowlisted full-line block. Runtime strings, regexes, marker text, imports, decorators, annotations, subprocess arguments, assertions, and test data remain byte/AST exact. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py` — 4 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_policy_decline_wins_over_a_bare_rejected`\n  - `D:test_invalid_object_is_its_own_kind_and_keeps_the_rebuild_recovery`\n  - `D:test_a_policy_decline_is_subtracted_from_both_retriable_predicates`\n- `tests/unit/store/test_merge_recovery.py` — 1 block:\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py` — 9 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_acquire_stamps_the_file_and_release_removes_it`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails`\n  - `D:test_release_unlinks_even_when_close_fails`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_MARKER_RE`\n  - `D:_acquire_offenders`\n  - `D:test_the_stamped_lock_acquire_appears_only_in_its_owner`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _tracker`\n  - `D:test_every_worker_still_excludes_a_second_holder_and_releases`\n- `tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py` — 8 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _canonical_store`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_a_symlinked_worktree_view_derives_the_canonical_stores_sidecars`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_a_plain_tracker_is_its_own_canonical`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_MARKER_RE`\n  - `D:test_the_tracker_sibling_rebar_derivation_appears_only_in_paths`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_every_real_sidecar_helper_lands_in_the_one_canonical_rebar`\n  - `D:test_every_real_sidecar_helper_lands_in_the_one_canonical_rebar`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is the maximal contiguous full-line comment block immediately before that unchanged code anchor. No other comment/docstring is editable.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Git outcome classification remains operation-sensitive; policy declines subtract from retriable predicates; invalid-object failures still trigger index rebuild; marker/timeout uniqueness guards retain their exact detection boundaries.\n- Merge recovery retains the shared mover's tracked/untracked, common-dir, vanished-path, and parser refusal fences, convergence behavior, and mandatory-reason escape.\n- Stamped locking retains release independence when close fails, bounded acquire/reclaim behavior, owner-exempt conjunction matching, mandatory-reason escape, and real-worker exclusion/release coverage.\n- Store paths retain canonical symlink resolution, plain/unreadable degradation, frozen derivations, tracker-sibling uniqueness, mandatory-reason escape, and end-to-end coverage of real sidecar helpers.\n- `tests/conftest.py` selects `/store/` and `test_stamped_lock` paths for the reduced macOS platform-compatibility lane; paths/module names remain unchanged.\n- These modules are otherwise collected directly by pytest. No `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found at the pinned base.\n\nPreserve these complete directive-bearing physical lines byte-for-byte:\n\n```python\n        return real_open(target, *args, **kwargs)  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        fd = real_open(target, *args, **kwargs)  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n        sp.tracker = \"/tmp/elsewhere\"  # type: ignore[misc]\n```\n\nAll other inline comments also remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Changes are limited to the 22 stable-ID prose blocks and adjacent blank lines; normalized-AST and token/comment comparisons pass for every owned path.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and preserves its listed constraint/consumer; historical narration, duplication, and separator ornament are removed.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] All 22 rows cite immutable blobs and record `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing/failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Focused pytest, scoped Ruff check/format, comment hygiene, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py tests/unit/store/test_merge_recovery.py tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/ruff check tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py tests/unit/store/test_merge_recovery.py tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/ruff format --check tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py tests/unit/store/test_merge_recovery.py tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `git diff --check -- tests/unit/store/test_git_outcome.py tests/unit/store/test_merge_recovery.py tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788618181546162001,"uuid":"0c5f06cd-08ae-494f-b2cb-4555be104fbe"}